1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
You understand English perfectly well, you can read it very easily, you listen and you understand everything clearly.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:13,000
But when you try to speak, you freeze.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Your mind is full, but your mouth stops.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
This is the biggest frustrations you face daily.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
You know the words, but they hide.

6
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
This is not a bad grammar problem.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
This is a physical tongue problem.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
And today, we will fix it completely.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Welcome to your 10-minute tongue training.

10
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
This training will change your English forever.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Close your eyes for a moment.

12
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Take a slow, deep breath. Let the air out gently.

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Picture a very familiar room.

14
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You are standing with other people.

15
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Someone looks directly at you.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:53,000
They ask you a simple small question.

17
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
They speak to you in English.

18
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
You know the exact answer perfectly.

19
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,000
You have the correct grammar side inside.

20
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You have the right vocabulary ready.

21
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
But then, something terrible happens.

22
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:09,000
You try to open your mouth.

23
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Your throat feels incredibly tight.

24
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Your heart starts to beat faster.

25
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Your palms begin to sweat.

26
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
You want to speak very clearly.

27
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,000
You really want to answer them.

28
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:25,000
But the words simply refuse to drop.

29
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Your mind holds the whole world.

30
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
But your mouth just stays closed.

31
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
You freeze in front of them all.

32
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
You smile an awkward, nervous smile.

33
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
You give a short, broken answer.

34
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Or worse, you just stay completely silent.

35
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Open your eyes right now.

36
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Does this exact memory hurt you?

37
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,000
It is a very painful experience.

38
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
It makes you feel incredibly small.

39
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:53,000
It makes you feel deeply embarrassed.

40
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
You walk away feeling angry with yourself.

41
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:58,000
You ask why can I not speak?

42
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Why is my English always so bad?

43
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Listen to me very carefully right now.

44
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:06,000
I need you to hear this honest truth.

45
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
You are not stupid at all.

46
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
You are not broken inside.

47
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Your English is not the real problem.

48
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,000
The real problem is how you were taught.

49
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,000
For years, you set quietly in classrooms.

50
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,000
You memorized thick, heavy textbooks.

51
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
You learned very difficult grammar rules.

52
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
You wrote long, boring essays.

53
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
You passed very hard written exams.

54
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:34,000
But nobody taught you how to speak.

55
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Nobody trained your mouth to move properly.

56
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
They gave you all the strict rules.

57
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
But they never gave you the real voice.

58
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
We live where English is a foreign language.

59
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
But we know it is a powerful bridge.

60
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
It is a wide gateway to big opportunities.

61
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:54,000
It connects us to the whole global world.

62
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Because of this, we feel heavy pressure.

63
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
We think we must be absolutely perfect.

64
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
We think making mistakes is a terrible crime.

65
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,000
But that exact pressure is what freezes you.

66
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
That pressure is quietly stealing your voice.

67
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:14,000
Today, we stop this terrible theft.

68
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Today, we change your story completely.

69
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
I know you dream of speaking beautifully.

70
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
You dream of talking without any hesitation.

71
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
You want your words to flow like water.

72
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
You want to stand tall in any room.

73
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
That dream is a very real possibility.

74
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
It is much closer than you think.

75
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:36,000
You do not need an expensive private tutor.

76
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,000
You do not need a fancy language academy.

77
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
You do not need years of hard study.

78
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:45,000
The secret is much simpler than that.

79
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
You really need to understand one clear thing.

80
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Your tongue is freezing because it is untrained.

81
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Your mind is fully ready for this.

82
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
But your mouth is simply not ready yet.

83
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,000
Millions of people share your exact pain.

84
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:02,000
They hide their voices just like you do.

85
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:05,000
But today, you step off that dark road.

86
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:08,000
You will stop fighting your busy mind.

87
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:11,000
You will start training your physical body.

88
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Just ten minutes a day is truly enough.

89
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:17,000
Ten minutes of focused tongue training.

90
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Daily, we are going to unlock your hidden voice.

91
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,000
We are going to break the heavy silence.

92
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Please stay with me right now.

93
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:29,000
Do not skip a single second of this.

94
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
This is the exact moment your life turns.

95
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Your journey to real confidence starts today.

96
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Let me tell you a secret today.

97
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:41,000
A very big, deeply important secret.

98
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Many people believe a very dangerous myth.

99
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:48,000
They look at fluent English speakers.

100
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
They see them speaking very confidently.

101
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
They hear the words flowing like water.

102
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
And they think that is pure magic.

103
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
They think that person has special talent.

104
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
They think I was not born with that gift.

105
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:05,000
Let me stop you right there.

106
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:07,000
Fluency is never a magic trick.

107
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Fluency is never a special hidden talent.

108
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Fluency is not a rare gift from birth.

109
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Fluency is simply a physical process.

110
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:20,000
It is a very predictable, normal process.

111
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,000
It is a muscle that needs daily training.

112
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Think about your own physical body.

113
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
Think about the strong muscles in your arms.

114
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Imagine you want to build strong arms.

115
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Do you sit and read a book about it?

116
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Do you memorize the rules of weightlifting?

117
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,000
No.

118
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Reading a book does absolutely nothing.

119
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Reading a book will never build muscle.

120
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,000
To build muscle.

121
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:48,000
You must lift heavy weights.

122
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,000
You must do the physical work daily.

123
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
You must physically move your real body.

124
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,000
Your tongue is exactly the same thing.

125
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Your tongue is a very strong active muscle.

126
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:03,000
It is the most important muscle for speech.

127
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
But you have never trained it properly.

128
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
You have only trained your quiet mind.

129
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:10,000
We learned English in a very strange way.

130
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
Our teachers gave us thick, heavy rule books.

131
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:16,000
They told us to memorize every single word.

132
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
They told us to translate silently in our heads.

133
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:23,000
We learned to process English very quietly.

134
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,000
We never learned to produce it out loud.

135
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:29,000
We never gave our tongue a real workout.

136
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Because of this, your mouth is out of shape.

137
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:37,000
It is completely starved of actual physical practice.

138
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
When you finally try to speak out loud,

139
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,000
your smart brain sends the correct signals.

140
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:46,000
But your tongue does not know how to move.

141
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,000
It feels heavy.

142
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
It feels very slow.

143
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
It trips over simple, very common words.

144
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
This is not a lack of intelligence.

145
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:57,000
This is a simple lack of physical movement.

146
00:06:57,000 --> 00:07:01,000
This is exactly why you need 10 minutes a day.

147
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Just 10 minutes of physical tongue training.

148
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
You do not need to learn new vocabulary.

149
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
You already know enough words to speak.

150
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
You do not need more complex grammar rules.

151
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:18,000
You already know the basics, standard rules.

152
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
You just need to connect the mind and mouth.

153
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
You need to bridge that quiet, empty gap.

154
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,000
You need to build physical muscle memory.

155
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Think about a professional winning athlete.

156
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
Think about a great famous stage singer.

157
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Do they perform without warming up first?

158
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
No.

159
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
They stretch their muscles every single day.

160
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
They prepare their physical bodies very carefully.

161
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
You must treat your voice the exact same way.

162
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:49,000
You must stretch your tongue daily.

163
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:52,000
You must condition your mouth to move freely.

164
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,000
10 minutes is a very small daily investment.

165
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:59,000
But it creates a massive life changing reward.

166
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:02,000
It breaks the invisible chains on your voice.

167
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Every single time you practice making sounds,

168
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
you are rewiring your deep brain pathways.

169
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,000
You are telling your nervous system it is safe.

170
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
You are telling your mind to relax completely.

171
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:18,000
When you train your tongue consistently,

172
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,000
something truly beautiful begins to happen.

173
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:24,000
The physical hesitation slowly melts away.

174
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:27,000
The heavy feeling leaves your tired mouth.

175
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:30,000
The words start to form much faster.

176
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
You stop translating from your mother tongue.

177
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:36,000
You start producing sounds directly and clearly.

178
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:39,000
You stop worrying about looking foolish.

179
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Because your mouth finally trusts your mind.

180
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
And your mind finally trusts your mouth.

181
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
This is the real true secret to fluency.

182
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:51,000
It is not about getting perfectly smart.

183
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:54,000
It is about getting physically prepared.

184
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
So, let go of the magic myth today.

185
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Stop waiting for a sudden miracle to happen.

186
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Stop feeling jealous of other fluent speakers.

187
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:07,000
They are not smarter than you are.

188
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:09,000
They just move their mouths more often.

189
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:12,000
They train their tongue muscles regularly.

190
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,000
And starting today, you will do exactly the same.

191
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:19,000
We are going to build that muscle together.

192
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:22,000
It will only take 10 minutes a day.

193
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Let us begin the real work today.

194
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,000
I am giving you a strict challenge.

195
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
It is a simple 30 day training challenge.

196
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
You must commit to this fully today.

197
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:36,000
You only need 10 minutes every morning.

198
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,000
You do not need a perfect room.

199
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:42,000
You do not need an audience watching.

200
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
You only need yourself and a mirror.

201
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:46,000
Are you ready to change your life?

202
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:49,000
Let us break down the exact steps.

203
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Phase one is about breaking the ice.

204
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Step one is facing your own reflection.

205
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Every morning walks straight to your mirror.

206
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
Stand up tall with your shoulders back.

207
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Look deep into your own tired eyes.

208
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Take a very slow, deep calming breath.

209
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
You must build trust with yourself first.

210
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:13,000
If you cannot face yourself alone securely,

211
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:16,000
you cannot face the noisy world outside.

212
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Start your daily timer for one minute.

213
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:22,000
This very first minute is your warm-up.

214
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Do not worry about making perfect sense.

215
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:28,000
Do not worry about correct grammar rules.

216
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Do not worry about your local accent.

217
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Just open your mouth and speak out.

218
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Say absolutely anything that comes to mind.

219
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Say your own name loud and clear.

220
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Talk about the sunny weather outside today.

221
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Describe what you will eat for breakfast.

222
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Talk about your big goals for today.

223
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Just make sure your tongue is moving.

224
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,000
At first, it will feel very strange.

225
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:57,000
You will feel silly talking to yourself.

226
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Your physical voice might sound very weak.

227
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Your nervous throat might feel quite tight.

228
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:06,000
You will hear all your own mistakes.

229
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Your scared mind will tell you to stop.

230
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:12,000
It will quietly say, this is useless.

231
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Ignore that negative inner voice completely today.

232
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
That dark voice is your old fear.

233
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
You are breaking that old fear now.

234
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
You are finally waking up the muscle.

235
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
This daily free talk is incredibly powerful.

236
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
It gently forces your brain to work.

237
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:34,000
It stops the slow, painful translation process.

238
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
You stop translating from your mother tongue.

239
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
You start producing English sounds instantly instead.

240
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
You are teaching your brain to relax.

241
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Mang2 is about deep physical stretching.

242
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Now, we flex the actual tongue muscle.

243
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,000
You will practice simple English tongue twisters.

244
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Do not try to speak fast today.

245
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Speed is never the main goal here.

246
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Clear pronunciation is what you are seeking.

247
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Say words that make your mouth work.

248
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
Stritting your closed lips wide and big.

249
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Make exaggerated funny faces in the mirror.

250
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Remember, nobody is watching you do this.

251
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
You are entirely safe in your room.

252
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:20,000
This physical movement is deeply, deeply important.

253
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
In our beautiful native South Asian languages,

254
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:27,000
our mouths move in a very specific way.

255
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:31,000
English requires very different daily muscle movements.

256
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:36,000
If you do not stretch these muscles, they will always feel stiff and slow.

257
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:39,000
This is exactly why you stumble often.

258
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:42,000
This is why words get trapped inside.

259
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
Tongue twisters force the muscle to wake.

260
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
They force your mouth into new shapes.

261
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Do this for one full, focused minute.

262
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Feel the real physical effort in your jaw.

263
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
Feel the tight stretch in your cheeks.

264
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
You are building real physical strength now.

265
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Just like a strong athlete in training.

266
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
You are conditioning your powerful speaking instrument.

267
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Do not stop if you make mistakes.

268
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
My mistakes are the actual proof of progress.

269
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Every single mistake makes your tongue stronger.

270
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:19,000
When you stumble, take a deep breath.

271
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Skart the sentence over from the beginning.

272
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Do not punish yourself for being imperfect.

273
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Treat yourself with deep kindness and patience.

274
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:32,000
This is just the first two minutes.

275
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
You are already changing your future path.

276
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:38,000
We will build the next steps together.

277
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Now we move to phase two today.

278
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,000
This is the true core of training.

279
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Your third minute is all about sounds.

280
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
We will focus on difficult English sounds.

281
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:53,000
These tiny sounds unlock your real fluency.

282
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:56,000
In our beautiful native South Asian languages,

283
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
we pronounce words in a different way.

284
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
We use different parts of the mouth.

285
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:04,000
English requires very specific new sound shapes.

286
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Think about sounds like T and H.

287
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Think about W and R and S.

288
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
These might seem like very minor details.

289
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:17,000
But they are deeply, deeply powerful tools.

290
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
When you master these specific sounds daily,

291
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:24,000
your whole accent changes very, very quickly.

292
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
You start sounding incredibly clear and sure.

293
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
You sound like someone who truly belongs.

294
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,000
You belong in any room, any conversation.

295
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Let us practice this together right now.

296
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Take the simple English word very today.

297
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:43,000
Many of us say wary instead normally,

298
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
because our tongue is confused by these fours

299
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
your top teeth onto your lip.

300
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Blow the air out slowly and softly.

301
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Feel the physical vibration in your mouth.

302
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:57,000
That is the actual muscle working hard.

303
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Now take the very common word.

304
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Think. Do not say it with a hard T.

305
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Put your tongue strictly between your teeth.

306
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Blow the air out gently and smoothly.

307
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Say the word think clearly and proudly.

308
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
You will immediately feel totally different inside.

309
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
You will sound like a confident person.

310
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:20,000
Let us look at another difficult sound.

311
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Look at the tricky English letter R.

312
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:25,000
We often roll our R very heavily.

313
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,000
We make it sound very hard indeed.

314
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
But English R is soft and round.

315
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Pull your tongue back inside your mouth.

316
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Do not let it touch the roof.

317
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Say the word river out loud now.

318
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Say it softly, smoothly and very cleanly.

319
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Practice your S blends with great care.

320
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Words like stop, smile and strong.

321
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Do not put an E before them.

322
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Do not say S stop or a smile.

323
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Ever Scott directly with the sharp S sound.

324
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:57,000
His like a small snake to start.

325
00:15:57,000 --> 00:16:01,000
These small corrections make a massive difference.

326
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:05,000
They separate frightened beginners from fluent speakers.

327
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Spend minutes three and four doing this.

328
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
Take a small list of difficult words.

329
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:14,000
Say them loudly in your quiet room.

330
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,000
Do not rush through this important step.

331
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Say the word world with careful precision.

332
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Say the word measure with deep focus.

333
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Train your tongue to find the shape.

334
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
At first, it will feel very unnatural.

335
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Your mouth will want to go back.

336
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
It will want its old comfortable habits.

337
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:38,000
But you must guide it very patiently.

338
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
You must teach it the new way.

339
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
This is exactly how athletes build muscle.

340
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:46,000
They repeat the exact same physical motion.

341
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
They do it hundreds of times daily.

342
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
You are doing the exact same thing.

343
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:55,000
You are building strong speech muscle memory.

344
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Mime and five and six are for combinations.

345
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Now you put those sounds into sentences.

346
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,000
Take a very short, simple English sentence.

347
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Write it out loud in your room.

348
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:09,000
But read it very, very slowly today.

349
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:12,000
Focus entirely on the exact mouth shapes.

350
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:15,000
Do not care about the deep meaning.

351
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Only care about how the sound feels.

352
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,000
When you speak clearly, people listen closely.

353
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:24,000
They stop asking you to repeat yourself.

354
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:27,000
When people ask, what did you say?

355
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Your fragile confidence breaks into tiny pieces.

356
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Your heart drops and you freeze again.

357
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,000
Clear sounds prevent this terrible painful moment.

358
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Clear sounds protect your growing self-belief.

359
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Soon your mouth will remember the shapes.

360
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:47,000
You will not have to think anymore.

361
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:52,000
When you stand in a crowded room, when someone asks you a tough question,

362
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,000
your mouth will automatically know the way.

363
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
It will not freeze in blind panic.

364
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
It will slide into the right position.

365
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
The words will form smoothly and clearly.

366
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Your ten minutes are building massive confidence.

367
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Let me share a true story today.

368
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:12,000
It is a small but powerful story.

369
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
It will show you what is possible.

370
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,000
I once met a young, bright girl.

371
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:21,000
She came from a small, quiet village.

372
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Her family was very modest and hardworking.

373
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
She was an incredibly smart, dedicated student.

374
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,000
But she carried a very heavy burden.

375
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
She walked up to me with sadness.

376
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:35,000
She looked down at the floor nervously.

377
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
She said to me in a quiet whisper.

378
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:41,000
I understand English perfectly when I hear it.

379
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:44,000
I can read thick books very easily.

380
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:49,000
But when I try to actually speak, my tongue completely freezes in my mouth.

381
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,000
I look like I do not know anything.

382
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
I feel so small and deeply ashamed.

383
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
People think I am not intelligent enough.

384
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
But my mind is full of answers.

385
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
I looked at her and smiled warmly.

386
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
I did not smile to mock her.

387
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
I smiled because I understood her completely.

388
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
I saw my own past deep struggles.

389
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:13,000
I felt the exact same pain once.

390
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
I told her to stop buying books.

391
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
I told her to stop memorizing words.

392
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:22,000
I told her to do one simple thing.

393
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Train your tongue before you check grammar.

394
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
She looked at me very confused initially.

395
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
She thought she needed more complex rules.

396
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,000
She thought she needed a magic formula.

397
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
But I promised her.

398
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
It was physical.

399
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:41,000
The 10 minute daily challenge she went back to her village home.

400
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:44,000
For 30 days, she faced her mirror.

401
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
She woke up early before her family.

402
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:49,000
She stood there while the house slept.

403
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:54,000
She spent 10 minutes every single morning.

404
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
She locked her door to feel safe.

405
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
She looked into her own frightened eyes.

406
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
She made strange sounds in her room.

407
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Her tongue felt very heavy and stiff.

408
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:09,000
She stretched her mouth wide open daily.

409
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,000
She practiced difficult, frustrating English sound shapes.

410
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,000
She spoke completely broken sentences out loud.

411
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
Her jaw ached from the new movements.

412
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
Her mind fought her every single day.

413
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,000
It told her she was wasting time.

414
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
But she remembered the deep, painful shame.

415
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
She never wanted to feel that again.

416
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
So she kept her promise to herself.

417
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Some days, she wanted to quit forever.

418
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
She felt very silly talking to herself.

419
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
But she ignored the fear of judgment.

420
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:46,000
She pushed through the awkward daily feeling.

421
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
One month later, she came back again.

422
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:51,000
I will never forget her beautiful face.

423
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Tears were streaming down her happy cheeks.

424
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:57,000
But they were not tears of sadness.

425
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
They were tears of pure, overwhelming joy.

426
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
She stood up tall and looked straight.

427
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
She did not look at the floor.

428
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:08,000
She spoke to me in clear English.

429
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
Her voice was steady.

430
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
Her words smooth.

431
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Her terrible hesitation was completely gone forever.

432
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:18,000
She said something I will always remember.

433
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
My English did not improve from books.

434
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:24,000
It improved because I moved my mouth.

435
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:27,000
I started practicing what I already knew.

436
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:31,000
That is the ultimate life-changing secret today.

437
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,000
She did not become a genius overnight.

438
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
She did not learn a thousand words.

439
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,000
She simply removed the heavy physical barrier.

440
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:43,000
She gave her tongue strength to move.

441
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
She stopped freezing and started flowing freely.

442
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Think about this brave young girl today.

443
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
She did not have a fancy background.

444
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:55,000
She did not have highly educated parents.

445
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:58,000
She did not have a perfect school.

446
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
She only had deep courage and consistency.

447
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:06,000
If she can break her heavy silence, then you can absolutely do the same.

448
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,000
Your situation is not impossible to fix.

449
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
You are facing the exact same wall.

450
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:14,000
And you have the exact same tool.

451
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:17,000
You do not need more useless information.

452
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:20,000
Your brain is already full of English.

453
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,000
You just need more simple mouth movement.

454
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:27,000
You need more clear, daily sound practice.

455
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:30,000
You need the courage to make mistakes.

456
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:34,000
You are full of beautiful, powerful thoughts.

457
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Do not let them die inside you.

458
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Give them the strong voice they deserve.

459
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:42,000
Her powerful story is now your story.

460
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:45,000
We have reached the final phase today.

461
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:48,000
You have warmed up in the mirror.

462
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:51,000
You have stretched your physical tongue muscles.

463
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,000
You have mastered the most difficult sounds.

464
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
Now, we bring it all fully together.

465
00:22:56,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Welcome to Minute 7, 8 and 9.

466
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
These three minutes are for reading loudly.

467
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Take a very simple, short English paragraph.

468
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Do not pick a difficult academic book.

469
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:12,000
Pick a simple story or news article.

470
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Hold it in your hands very proudly.

471
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Now, read it out loud to yourself.

472
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:20,000
But do not just read it quietly.

473
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Do not read it like a board robot.

474
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Write it with huge exaggerated human emotion.

475
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:29,000
If the sentence is happy, smile widely.

476
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
The sentence is sad.

477
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,000
It sounds serious.

478
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,000
If it is exciting, raise your voice.

479
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:38,000
You must connect your feelings to words.

480
00:23:38,000 --> 00:23:41,000
English is not just a dead subject.

481
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:44,000
It is a living, breathing human language.

482
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,000
When you inject real emotion into words,

483
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:50,000
your brain remembers them so much faster,

484
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,000
your mouth learns the rhythm of speech.

485
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:56,000
You stop sounding like a nervous student.

486
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:59,000
You start sounding like a confident speaker.

487
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Write loudly for three full uninterrupted minutes.

488
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Do not stop to check your dictionary.

489
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:08,000
Do not stop if you pronounce something wrong.

490
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:11,000
Just keep moving forward with strong energy.

491
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:14,000
Let the English words flow out fully.

492
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:17,000
You are building incredible momentum right now.

493
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:19,000
You are teaching your mouth to flow.

494
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:22,000
You are connecting the mind and tongue.

495
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Now we reached the very last minute.

496
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:27,000
Many number ten is the most magical.

497
00:24:27,000 --> 00:24:30,000
Put your reading paper completely away now.

498
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:33,000
Stand perfectly still in your quiet room.

499
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:36,000
Close your eyes gently for one minute.

500
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Breathe deeply into your chest once more.

501
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:42,000
Now simply listen to your own mind.

502
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:44,000
Listen to your inner voice.

503
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Speaking English, imagine yourself.

504
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:49,000
Standing in a big meeting.

505
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,000
Imagine answering a very difficult interview question.

506
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:56,000
See yourself speaking with complete, total ease.

507
00:24:56,000 --> 00:25:00,000
Your inner voice completely shapes your reality.

508
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:03,000
If your inner voice is deeply afraid,

509
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:06,000
your outer voice will shake and tremble.

510
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:09,000
But if your inner voice is totally confident,

511
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:13,000
your outer voice will be entirely unshakable.

512
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:16,000
When your inner and outer voice is aligned,

513
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:20,000
unbreakable confidence is finally born in society.

514
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,000
Do not underestimate these simple ten minutes.

515
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:27,000
They are quietly rewiring your whole brain.

516
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:30,000
They are strongly conditioning your physical tongue.

517
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:34,000
They are slowly dissolving your deep hesitation.

518
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:38,000
There is a reason professional singers practice.

519
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:42,000
They practice every single morning without fail.

520
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:46,000
There is a reason professional athletes stretch.

521
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,000
There is a reason great speakers prepare.

522
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:52,000
Proper preparation is never an optional thing.

523
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:56,000
Your daily preparation is this ten minute training.

524
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:00,000
When you practice daily, something beautiful happens.

525
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:03,000
English stops feeling like a terrifying test.

526
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:06,000
It starts feeling like a completely normal habit.

527
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:09,000
A skill grows every time you practice.

528
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:12,000
A skill dies every time you quit.

529
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:16,000
The real difference between success and failure is

530
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:20,000
never about having natural raw talent.

531
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:23,000
It is always about having absolute consistency.

532
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:27,000
You cannot exercise once and expect strength.

533
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:31,000
You cannot practice occasionally and expect fluency.

534
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:35,000
But ten minutes daily changes absolutely everything.

535
00:26:35,000 --> 00:26:39,000
Because small daily effort builds on itself.

536
00:26:39,000 --> 00:26:43,000
Your deep courage compounds every single morning.

537
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:46,000
You do not need a perfect environment.

538
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:49,000
You do not need entirely flawless grammar.

539
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:52,000
You do not need an enormous vocabulary.

540
00:26:52,000 --> 00:26:56,000
All you truly need is quiet courage.

541
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:59,000
You need consistency and very firm belief.

542
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:02,000
You must firmly believe you are capable.

543
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Picture your beautiful future self right now.

544
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:09,000
Speaking with great ease in important meetings.

545
00:27:09,000 --> 00:27:13,000
Walking into interviews without any blind panic.

546
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:17,000
Traveling the world without any language barriers.

547
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:21,000
Expressing your best ideas with absolute clarity.

548
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:24,000
That amazing person is not far away.

549
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:27,000
That person already lives deep inside you.

550
00:27:27,000 --> 00:27:30,000
Ten minutes a day is your investment.

551
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:33,000
A completely new you is the reward.

552
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:37,000
You will face days of deep discouragement.

553
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:40,000
There will be mornings when you feel tired.

554
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:42,000
People around you might suddenly laugh.

555
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:45,000
Someone may mock how you pronounce words.

556
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:48,000
Someone may ask why you are practicing.

557
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
They might say who are you impressing?

558
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:54,000
When this happens, you will feel hurt.

559
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:57,000
You will feel a deep, heavy shame.

560
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Your old fear will tell you to hide.

561
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:01,000
You will want to quit right there.

562
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:03,000
But you must hold on to truth.

563
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:06,000
You are not doing this for them.

564
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:08,000
You are not trying to impress anyone.

565
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:11,000
You are doing this for your future.

566
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:13,000
You are doing it for your confidence.

567
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:16,000
People who laugh simply do not understand.

568
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:19,000
They do not understand real personal growth.

569
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:22,000
They are stuck in their own fears.

570
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:25,000
Leave them behind in their quiet comfort.

571
00:28:25,000 --> 00:28:28,000
You must change your mindset right now.

572
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Stop saying my English is very bad.

573
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:35,000
Stop saying I am completely terrified.

574
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:38,000
Stop assuming people will always judge you.

575
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:41,000
You must shift your internal words today.

576
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:44,000
You must say I am proudly learning.

577
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:48,000
You must say I am getting much better.

578
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:53,000
When a small child learns to speak, they make mistakes every single day.

579
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:56,000
They mispronounce very simple, easy words.

580
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:59,000
They repeat things entirely the wrong way.

581
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:01,000
Do their parents tell them to stop?

582
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:04,000
Do they say you are not perfect?

583
00:29:04,000 --> 00:29:07,000
No, they cheer for every small sound.

584
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:10,000
They celebrate the brave effort of trying.

585
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:12,000
You must be that parent to yourself.

586
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Give yourself strict permission to be imperfect.

587
00:29:16,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Let your tongue practice without any judgment.

588
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Let your daily progress be wonderfully slow.

589
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Broken English spoken with brave, strong couragees.

590
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Worth much more than silent perfection.

591
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Perfect English trapped behind heavy fear is useless.

592
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:38,000
Fluency does not come from studying books.

593
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Fluency comes from making loud sounds daily.

594
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:44,000
The world belongs to those who rise.

595
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:47,000
It belongs gone to those who try again.

596
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:50,000
No matter how many times they fall,

597
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:53,000
every great speaker was once truly terrified.

598
00:29:53,000 --> 00:29:57,000
Every confident person once doubted themselves deeply.

599
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:01,000
Every fluent speaker stumbled over simple words.

600
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:05,000
Your specific journey is beautifully your own.

601
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:08,000
You are not behind anyone else today.

602
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,000
You are exactly where you need to be.

603
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:13,000
But you must make a firm decision.

604
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Will you stay silent in the dark shadows?

605
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:19,000
Or will you rise and finally speak?

606
00:30:19,000 --> 00:30:21,000
I want you to promise me something.

607
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:23,000
No, promise it to yourself.

608
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Repeat these exact words out loud now.

609
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Do not whisper.

610
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Say them very loudly.

611
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:32,000
Say them with fire in your chest.

612
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:35,000
I am not afraid of mistakes anymore.

613
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,000
I will not hide my real voice.

614
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:40,000
I am fully capable of doing this.

615
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:42,000
I will not stop my daily practice.

616
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:45,000
My voice truly deserves to be heard.

617
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:48,000
I will not quit on myself ever.

618
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Say it again with absolute raw power.

619
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,000
I am not afraid anymore.

620
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:56,000
I will not stop my training.

621
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:59,000
The long waiting is finally over now.

622
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:02,000
Your heavy excuses are completely dead today.

623
00:31:02,000 --> 00:31:04,000
You do not need anyone special permission.

624
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:07,000
You do not need their small approval.

625
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:10,000
You only need the courage to begin.

626
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:13,000
And your beautiful journey starts right today.

627
00:31:13,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Do not wait for a perfect tomorrow.

628
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:17,000
Go to your mirror right now.

629
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:20,000
Start your very first 10 focused minutes.

630
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,000
Speak bravely.

631
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Practice hard.

632
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Train your tongue.

633
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:27,000
Watch what happens to your whole life.

634
00:31:27,000 --> 00:31:31,000
I believe in you completely and truly.

635
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:34,000
And very soon the whole world will listen.

636
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:38,000
They will hear your undeniably powerful voice.

637
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:42,000
The confident, fluent, beautiful voice of you.

